# task-64b74fc5 later-instance failed evidence (7x7 test)

Test was uniform horizontal rows `[0,9,3,6,9,8,0]`. Eight demos were provided, eight submissions failed. No solution was validated.

Important latest pair: demo 8 (26x26) has full-width bands in input at rows 5=9, 6=7, 8=2, 11=9, 12=9, 18=1, 19=2, 22=2, 25=7. Output rows show a complex row cycle beginning `[1,2,9,9,2,9,7,7,2,1,2,9,9,2,9,7,7,2,...]`; full grid has period-like 18 row signature and preserves non-background colors as part of a sequence.

Prior demos were very different, including periodic full-width row patterns and diagonal encodings. Failed test submissions:
1. period 3 diagonal cycle [2,6,6], r-c;
2. test-row sequence indexed r-c mod 7;
3. unchanged input;
4. repeated period-3 [2,6,6];
5. test-row sequence indexed r+c;
6. same with offset +1;
7. r+c without offset;
8. repeated r+c.
All rejected. If task returns, do not recycle these. Derive the encoding mapping from multiple demos and reproduce them exactly; current rule unknown.
